    <artifactId>kompile-app-ingest-svc</artifactId>
    <name>Kompile App - Ingest Service Layer</name>
    <description>
        Step 3 of the services decomposition: the document-ingest service layer extracted from
        kompile-app-main. Carries the two largest god-classes in the old services package —
        DocumentIngestService and VectorStorePopulationService — plus the ingest orchestration
        around them (staged pipeline, chunk dedup/enrichment, contextual RAG config, cross-document
        relation extraction, cross-index tracking, index status/sync, freshness, job resume, progress
        trackers, adaptive batching + audit, Confluence/YouTube/markdown source conversion) and the
        subprocess launch machinery those services drive (SubprocessIngestLauncher,
        VectorPopulationSubprocessLauncher, and the shared subprocess config/command/lifecycle/output/
        restart/handle types every other launcher in app-main also uses).

        Sits above platform/ingest/crawl/mcp in the layering. Verified zero back-edges into
        kompile-app-main: the two that existed were inverted — SubprocessHeartbeatBroadcaster moved
        down into kompile-app-platform, and MonitorService is reached through the
        SubprocessTaskCompletionListener SPI (also in platform, implemented by app-main).

        This module is what lets the crawl/ingest web controllers move out of app-main into a persona
        app without dragging the admin console along. Package names preserved
        (ai.kompile.app.services.*) so native-image reflect/resource config and the many in-app
        importers are unaffected.

        See docs/architecture/services-decomposition-spec.md and
        docs/architecture/app-persona-boundary.md.
    </description>

